                ;
                ; On a target whose `int` is 32 bits (Kotlin, Java, C#, Scala)
                ; a millisecond stamp does not fit, so the value is its low 32
                ; bits. That is still a number that changes whenever the file
                ; changes, which is all a staleness check reads it for; it is
                ; not a wall-clock time on those four.
