        ; amortized-O(len(suffix)) grow; immutable-string targets lower it to
        ; `a = a + b`, one copy, which is what they would spell anyway. The
        ; interpreter's slot machinery drives `s += "..."` through it once a
        ; binding's string is proven unshared.
